// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: CALLED but never assigned
// BUG-864: the LOCAL declaration site rejects an uninitialised funcptr; the
// GLOBAL site had no such arm, so this was accepted and `g_cb(5)` jumped
// through NULL. On bare metal address 0 is routinely mapped, so the jump
// SUCCEEDS into whatever lives there — silent at compile time and at run time.
//
// The rule deliberately is NOT "a global funcptr needs an initializer": that
// was measured and BACKED OUT because it rejects the callback-registry idiom
// (see tests/zer/funcptr_global_registry_ok.zer). Only "called and never
// assigned anywhere in the file" is unambiguous.
*(u32) -> u32 g_cb;
u32 main() { return g_cb(5); }
